# runs/ is gitignored EXCEPT the committed results: the summary CSVs, the
# figures the README embeds (a gitignored figure is a broken image on GitHub),
# and the diagnostic and distribution JSONs that the headline claims in
# README §5.4 rest on. Both are small (~360 KB each set) and neither is
# regenerable without the checkpoints and an hour of GPU time.
runs/*
!runs/results/
runs/results/*
!runs/results/*.csv
!runs/results/*.png
!runs/diag/
runs/diag/*
!runs/diag/*.json
!runs/dist/
runs/dist/*
!runs/dist/*.json

# data/ IS committed. The corpus swap moved the headline by ~5x, so the exact
# document set is part of the result, not an input that can be regenerated.
# See data/README.md and LIMITATIONS.md §18.

.venv/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.memmap
